description:
FILED s543e (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-21) while fixing #1030 (the %ENV value layer).  PRE-EXISTING (identical on the base extraction e1e53f96).  SILENT.

REPRODUCER (scratch/s543e/p1/localenv.pl in the s543e worktree):
    $ENV{LA} = "outer";
    {
      local %ENV = (LB => "inner");
      print "in: LA=[", ($ENV{LA} // 'U'), "] LB=[", ($ENV{LB} // 'U'), "]\n";
      system('echo "in child: LA=[$LA] LB=[$LB]"');
    }
    print "out: LA=[", ($ENV{LA} // 'U'), "] LB=[", ($ENV{LB} // 'U'), "]\n";
    system('echo "out child: LA=[$LA] LB=[$LB]"');

  perl 5.40.3:  in: LA=[U] LB=[inner] / in child: LA=[] LB=[inner] / out: LA=[outer] LB=[U] / out child: LA=[outer] LB=[]
  PCL:          in: LA=[U] LB=[inner] / in child: LA=[outer] LB=[]  / (out = perl)

The program's OWN reads are right; a CHILD process started inside the `local` sees the OUTER environment.  `local %ENV = (...)` (or `local %ENV; $ENV{X} = ...`) to run a child with a controlled environment is the idiom it breaks.

MECHANISM: `local %ENV = LIST` is emitted as a CL special binding of the variable `%ENV` to a fresh hash TABLE: `(let ((%ENV (p-copy-hash (p-flatten-args (list %ENV "PR" 1))))) ...)` -- so inside the scope %ENV is an ordinary hash and no store reaches the process environment.  perl localises the hash WITH its env magic (mg_localize), so the new hash's stores still setenv, and the restore puts the old values back.

FIX SHAPE (untried): the `local %ENV` lowering must keep the MARKER: save the whole environment (and the #1030 undef marks, `*p-env-undef-keys*`), clear it, run the LIST assignment through the marker's `%ENV = LIST` arm, and restore the saved environment on exit (unwind-protect) -- a runtime macro `p-local-env` the `local %h` lowering selects when the hash is `%ENV` (a core variable, not a module name: rule 9a allows it).  Measure first where `local %NAME` is lowered (Pl/ExprToCL.pm / Parser2 `local` arm) and whether `local %INC` has the same shape (it would bind %INC to a table too: probe `local %INC; require X`).

NOT the same mechanism as #1030 (that one is the element store; this one is the emission of `local` for the whole hash), so it was not forced into s543e.
